Gehennom is pretty easy; as long as you've got a decent ascenscion kit, you'll 
get by. Once you wake up the Wizard of Yendor, however, you'll want things 
optimal. So, map out and collect items from all the levels of Gehennom before 
you do so. Mark the vibrating square, dig a path between the stairs on each 
level, etc. As for what to carry, well, going by category:

     Gold: Donate it all for protection.
     Weapons: Whatever you're going to wield and quiver. Don't bring anything you
won't use.
     Armor: T-shirt, silver dragin scale mail, cloak of magic resistance,
gauntlets of dexterity, helm of brilliance, speed boots, shield. Enchant as much
as possible.
     Potions: A couple potions of full healing, and some holy water in a sack.
Polypile and alchemize the rest to increase your max HP and power.
     Scrolls: Four scrolls of gold detection, to read confused while on the
planes to find the portals. Polypile the rest into charging (to read confused),
enchant armor and enchant weapon.
     Wands: All your wands of death, for Rodney. One wand of cancellation, in
case your bag of holding gets cursed. Optionally, a wand of lightning to engrave
Elbereth, and some wands of digging for the plane of earth.
     Rings: levitation, conflict, slow digestion
     Tools: unicorn horn, bag of holding, skeleton key
     Amulets: An amulet of reflection if you need it, and all the amulets of life
saving you can get your hands on, especially for a first ascenscion.
     Gems: Leave them by the stairs on level 1. If you want them, get them when
you're coming up.
     Spellbooks: Essentials only - magic missile, dig, finger of death, magic
mapping, detect treasure. Leave the rest by the stairs on level 1.
     Comestibles: A lizard corpse in your main inventory, some C- and K-rations
in your bag. Take out the rations before you face Famine.

Beyond that, just don't get burdened. Extra items can't hurt, and they might
help.
